Z||000000||Jake_Dragon||02-24-2001||07:47 PM||||This is about an 85-sport coupe 2.5L I have recently acquired.<BR>I am having power problems and need advice.<BR>When I start the car it idles real high 2000.<BR>After the car warms up it wants to die if I put it in gear.<BR>I also loose power if I turn on the vent or AC.<BR>If I am sitting idling in gear and turn on the vent or ac it will die.<P>I have replace:<BR>Idle Air Control Valve (New)<BR>Injector (New)<BR>Fuel filter (New)<BR>Fuel pump (New)<BR>Distributor (New)<BR>Cap and Rotor (New)<BR>Wires (New)<P>I am considering the EGR<P>What else should I check?<BR> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif"> <p>[This message has been edited by Jake_Dragon (edited 02-25-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||sqoach||02-24-2001||08:57 PM||||mine also idles high at start up. but i think that's normal on older cars. anyway, if you turn on the a/c and it loses power, sounds like an alternator problem. maybe a loose belt.<P>i would have the alternator checked as your next step. if you need to replace it, i have one i'll sell to you.<P>------------------<BR>sqoach@yahoo.com<P>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mysig2.JPG"> <BR>84 SE (project car?)<BR>85 Coupe (parts car)<BR>86 SC (daily driver)||||reg||1
Z||000002||DRJAGUAR||02-24-2001||09:05 PM||||I agree .. Check the Altinator. Had this problem with my 85 4 cyl a few times.<P>------------------<BR>85 2.8R (R=ROCKET) 4Spd.<BR>Wanna Race???||||reg||1
Z||000003||Rodrv6||02-24-2001||10:41 PM||||You might want to take a look at your idle air controller.  If it is gummed up or not working properly it can cause the symptoms you have.<P>------------------<BR>Rod Schneider, Woodstock, Ga.  84 SE, 330,000 miles and counting, 88 GT, not nearly as many miles :)||||reg||1
